From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:54:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: keep the CPU idle hint in
 suspend-to-idle

The gs101 CPU PM notifier stops writing the per-CPU power-down hint
(CPU_INFORM) once suspend_noirq has run, so that the last CPU going
through a firmware system suspend doesn't overwrite the system sleep
hint with C2.

Suspend-to-idle has no such sequence: the CPUs keep entering their
cpuidle states, and the firmware refuses a CPU power-down that has no
hint. Every idle entry then fails at once and the CPUs spin on refused
PSCI calls until a wakeup, drawing more than an idle system that is
awake.

Only ignore CPU_PM_ENTER when the suspend target is not s2idle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
index 1e7769db9..27e9ae20c 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/reboot.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 
 #include <linux/soc/samsung/exynos-regs-pmu.h>
@@ -601,6 +602,15 @@ static int exynos_pmu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static int exynos_cpupm_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
+	/*
+	 * In suspend-to-idle the CPUs keep entering their cpuidle states and
+	 * nothing else programs the PMU for them, so they still need the
+	 * per-CPU hint: without it the firmware refuses every power-down and
+	 * the idle loop spins on refused PSCI calls until wakeup.
+	 */
+	if (pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE)
+		return 0;
+
 	raw_spin_lock(&pmu_context->cpupm_lock);
 	pmu_context->sys_insuspend = true;
 	raw_spin_unlock(&pmu_context->cpupm_lock);
